 kind of personal pension  accounts or things like that  so you see the pain almost immediately  um in this particular circumstance i  mean that contestant election  or just the fact of a delayed election  could have uh  more time to begin with and take an even  bigger  hit on stocks just given the uncertainty  that we're in so far  right and looking a little bit more  closely at the results that are coming  in tonight  how could uh swing states impact the  markets  as we head into uh this time where we  may not have  a clear answer on who the winner is well  that's a great question  florida is definitely in the spotlight  and that's a big one that people are  watching north carolina  ohio pennsylvania even so a lot of these  swing states are actually coming  um out shortly uh if they haven't  already actually haven't looked at my  screens but  those are really going to change how the  market is viewing the possibility  of a trump victory now going into  tonight you really saw the markets  go all in on a blue wave trade so that  means really  going forward for cyclical stocks for  the oil sector  for people that could benefit from a  buyer's containment measure from that  additional stimulus so a lot of those  small businesses a lot of the small cap  stocks  that really need that additional funding  airlines even are another example so  going into tonight you really saw the  market positioning for that  but then once again um if it all flips  because the swing states that  shows up in the markets immediately you  see those risk gauges pull back you say  hold on a second  we shouldn't be running too fast and  you've already seen that happen a few  times uh just in the last few hours  and you mentioned the importance of the  impact of the winner on  these specific sectors but uh more  specifically looking at how it could  just impact  our viewers wallets what are some of the  things that either candidate if they win  could be doing that could influence our  money  tha